<LegalLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Information about browser storage, external website services, and the current use of analytics and advertising technologies on the Belaro Precision website.">
  <h2>1. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small pieces of information stored by a browser. Similar technologies include local storage and session storage. These are distinct from ordinary requests used to load a page, font or image, which can still disclose technical information such as an IP address to a service provider.</p>
  <h2>2. Current website functionality</h2>
  <p>The website’s own navigation, component selection links and enquiry form do not set first-party analytics or advertising cookies or use local storage to save form details. The form sends information when you submit it; browser autofill behaviour is controlled by your browser.</p>
  <p>Hosting and security services may process technical request information and may use necessary security technologies depending on their configuration. When enabled on the enquiry form, Cloudflare Turnstile processes browser signals to help detect automated abuse. Its behaviour may vary with the security configuration. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>3. Fonts and images</h2>
  <p>Google Fonts and some Unsplash images are loaded from external servers. Loading these resources causes your browser to contact those providers; an external request is not itself evidence of an advertising cookie. For more information, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://unsplash.com/privacy">Unsplash’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>4. Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>This website currently does not load Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, Google Ads conversion tracking or remarketing tags. It does not currently provide optional analytics or advertising cookie settings.</p>
  <p>If these technologies are introduced, this notice will need to reflect the services used and the relevant consent choices will need to be provided before optional technologies are activated where consent is required.</p>
  <h2>5. Your browser controls</h2>
  <p>You can use your browser’s privacy settings to inspect, block or delete cookies and site data. The steps depend on the browser. Blocking security features or external resources may affect the enquiry form or page appearance. Deleting browser data does not delete an enquiry already sent to us.</p>
  <h2>6. Further information</h2>
  <p>Read our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for enquiry data, technical files and information requests. If you have questions about a browser request or stored item associated with this website, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> with the page and service involved.</p>
</LegalLayout>
